Installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for this project.

## Changes Made:

### 1. Installed Package
- Installed `@vercel/speed-insights` package using npm
- Updated package.json and package-lock.json with the new dependency

### 2. Added SpeedInsights Component
- Modified `src/App.tsx` to import and use the SpeedInsights component
- Added import: `import { SpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights/react";`
- Added `<SpeedInsights />` component alongside the existing `<Analytics />` component

### Implementation Details:
- Followed the official Vercel Speed Insights documentation for React/Vite projects
- Used the React-specific import path: `@vercel/speed-insights/react`
- Placed the component in the root App component, similar to the existing Analytics component
- The component will automatically track and report Web Vitals to Vercel

### Framework Context:
- Project uses Vite + React + TypeScript
- SpeedInsights component is placed at the root level of the component tree to ensure proper tracking across all routes
- The implementation follows the same pattern as the existing Vercel Analytics integration

### Verification:
- ✅ Build completed successfully (npm run build)
- ✅ All tests passed (npm run test - 12 tests)
- ✅ No TypeScript compilation errors
- ✅ Lock file properly updated

### Next Steps:
To enable Speed Insights on Vercel:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Navigate to the Speed Insights section in the Vercel dashboard
3. Click the Enable button
4. The Speed Insights script will automatically be injected and begin collecting data

